TITLE:: RCCurve
summary:: A voice's curved course: one envelope per coordinate over the note, fitted, sliced, sent to a synth
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCLines, Classes/RCLineControl, Classes/Env

DESCRIPTION::
A line of link::Classes/RCLines:: glides each coordinate straight from its code::from:: value to its code::to:: value. A curved line also carries code::path::: an Event key → link::Classes/Env:: whose times are fractions of the note (summing to 1) and whose curves are sclang's envelope curves (a number per segment, 0 linear). A key without an Env stays straight and costs nothing more.

A synth reads a path at an index, the fraction of the line, from a control array of link::#*maxPoints:: breakpoints, code::<key>_env:: (link::Classes/IEnvGen::'s data), switched on by code::<key>_curved::; a warped index re-times the whole course (the time mode of link::Classes/RCAttractor::); through a gliding release the coordinate goes on along its end tangent, code::<key>_tail:: (units per line length). link::#*course:: and link::#*glide:: build that inside a SynthDef; link::#*eventControls:: sets the controls on a note's event.

code::
~env = RCCurve.fit({ |s| s.squared });       // a curve of s in 0..1 → at most 8 breakpoints
RCCurve.at(~env, 0.5);                       // ≈ 0.25
RCCurve.serverArray(~env);                   // the 32 values of <key>_env
RCCurve.lineFrom([[0, (pitch: 0)], [1, (pitch: 0.2)], [2, (pitch: 1)]], 3);   // a line with its path
::

The fit, the slice and the server array were the HadronLake3 Texture rig's; they are shared here by the Texture and Surfaces rigs.

CLASSMETHODS::

subsection:: Settings

METHOD:: maxPoints
Breakpoints of the synths' control arrays: 8 (7 segments), 32 values.

METHOD:: tolerance
The fit's error, as a fraction of the curve's excursion: 0.02.

METHOD:: numSamples
Samples of a Function fitted: 32.

subsection:: Paths

METHOD:: env
An Env from levels, times (any unit: scaled to fractions of 1) and curves (numbers, 0 linear).
argument:: levels
argument:: times
argument:: curves

METHOD:: at
The value of a path at strong::s:: in 0..1; a nil path is the straight line from strong::a:: to strong::b::.
argument:: env
argument:: s
argument:: a
argument:: b

METHOD:: curveAt
One envelope segment's value at strong::pos:: in 0..1 by sclang's curve rule: code::a + (b - a) (1 - e^(c pos)) / (1 - e^c)::, linear for c near 0.
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: c
argument:: pos

METHOD:: curveThrough
The curvature taking a segment from strong::a:: to strong::b:: through the midpoint value strong::m::, or nil when no monotone segment passes there.
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: m

METHOD:: fit
Fit a curve into at most strong::n:: breakpoints: the two ends first, each segment given the curvature through its sampled midpoint, the worst segment split while its error exceeds strong::tol:: × the excursion. Returns an Env (times as fractions), or nil for a flat curve.
argument:: curve
A Function of s in 0..1, or an Array of samples equally spaced in s.
argument:: n
Defaults to link::#*maxPoints::.
argument:: tol
Defaults to link::#*tolerance::.
argument:: samples
Samples of a Function; defaults to link::#*numSamples::.

METHOD:: slice
A path's part between strong::s0:: and strong::s1::, its times renormalised.
argument:: env
argument:: s0
argument:: s1

METHOD:: cut
The part before strong::s::.
argument:: env
argument:: s

METHOD:: reflect
The path's breakpoints past a wall mirrored back inside (link::Classes/RCLaws#*reflect::).
argument:: env
argument:: lo
argument:: hi

METHOD:: clip
The path's breakpoints held at the walls.
argument:: env
argument:: lo
argument:: hi

METHOD:: mapLevels
Every level through code::offset + scale * x::: an affine map keeps each segment's shape exactly (a coupling of one coordinate to another, a gain in dB).
argument:: env
argument:: scale
argument:: offset

METHOD:: peak
The highest level (each segment is monotone: its extremes are its ends).
argument:: env

METHOD:: endSlope
The slope at the end in units per line length: the tangent a gliding release goes on along. A padded segment of no length is skipped.
argument:: env

METHOD:: isCurved
True when a path bends: more than two breakpoints, or one curved segment.
argument:: env

METHOD:: serverArray
The control array a synth plays, IEnvGen's raw data read at an index (the fraction of the line): code::[offset, first level, segments, total, (time, shape 5, curve, level) per segment]::, the path's times as fractions (a hand-made Env's normalised), padded to strong::n:: - 1 segments by flat ones of length 1 past the end (an index beyond 1 holds the last level). A path with more breakpoints is refitted.
argument:: env
argument:: lineDur
No longer used (the index carries the line's time); kept for the callers.
argument:: n
Defaults to link::#*maxPoints::.

subsection:: Lines

METHOD:: lineFrom
A line from time-ordered samples code::[[time, params], ...]::: from the first sample to the last, every key whose values bend fitted into its path (resampled evenly in time first), a straight or constant key carrying none. A course shorter than strong::minDur:: gives the straight line between its ends stretched to minDur (link::Classes/RCLines#*between::'s chirp). nil for fewer than two samples.
argument:: samples
argument:: id
argument:: minDur
Defaults to link::Classes/RCLines#*defaultMinDur::.
argument:: n
argument:: tol

subsection:: In a SynthDef

METHOD:: controls
The controls of a curved coordinate, an Event: code::env:: (code::<key>_env::), code::curved:: (code::<key>_curved::), code::tail:: (code::<key>_tail::).
argument:: key

METHOD:: course
A coordinate along its line at strong::index:: (0 at the note, 1 at the line's end, beyond it through a gliding release; a warped index re-times the course): straight from strong::a:: to strong::b::, or the path read at the index (IEnvGen), followed by its end tangent.
argument:: key
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: index

METHOD:: glide
A coordinate gliding from strong::a:: to strong::b:: over strong::dur:: seconds, started again by strong::trig:: (a continuous grain's next target on a running synth): the straight EnvGen line, or its path read at link::#*glideIndex::; the flag picks.
argument:: key
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: dur
argument:: trig

METHOD:: glideIndex
How far a glide is: 0 → 1 over strong::dur:: seconds, held at 1, started again by strong::trig::.
argument:: dur
argument:: trig

subsection:: In a template

METHOD:: eventControls
Set a note event's path controls for strong::keys:: from a hit's path: a curved key gets code::<key>_env:: (its server array, wrapped once: one control array, not one synth per value) and code::<key>_curved:: 1, with strong::withTails:: also code::<key>_tail:: and code::<key>_peak::; every other key gets code::<key>_curved:: 0 (a straight line after a curved one on the same synth turns its envelope off). Returns the event.
argument:: ev
argument:: path
argument:: keys
argument:: lineDur
argument:: withTails

EXAMPLES::

code::
// a voice's course sampled along an arc, its path, the event a synth would get
(
var samples = 9.collect { |i| var t = i / 2; [t, (pitch: (t - 2).squared / 4, az: 0.3 * t)] };
var line = RCCurve.lineFrom(samples, 0);
line.postln;
RCCurve.eventControls((), line[\path], [\pitch, \az], 4).postln;
)
::
